    {
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Most likely differences in how you handle the split.\r\n\r\nMost libraries have defaults to cut the range of the BPE (which otherwise makes the algorithm O(n\u00b2)). `tokenizers` does not make a choice for you as there are mutliple ways to go about that (most used is whitespace splitting, other would be limiting token size, but in general whatever goes in `pre_tokenizer`).\r\nThe is most likely the cause you're seeing this. Adding a relevant `pre_tokenizer` should fix your issue.\r\n\r\nThen `tokenizers` uses `u32` which might trigger some overflows (just so that you know). (Don't know about youtokentome).\r\nLarger training set will require `u64` which in general will be slower than `u32`, and `tokenizers` doesn't support that at the moment.",
      "created_at": "2023-08-07T09:01:41Z",
